WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:04.000
<i>My first champion
and the love of my life</i>

00:04.210 --> 00:05.670
<i>was Maya, my wife.</i>

00:05.840 --> 00:08.260
<i>Her tragic crash destroyed me.</i>

00:08.430 --> 00:12.220
<i>I let myself go completely
and left everything behind,</i>

00:12.390 --> 00:14.720
<i>even my young daughter, Eva.</i>

00:15.850 --> 00:18.100
<i>I resurfaced
but never looked back.</i>

00:18.350 --> 00:20.020
<i>The past was the past.</i>

00:20.230 --> 00:22.360
<i>The stress
of the Great Race of Oban</i>

00:22.520 --> 00:24.780
<i>dredged up these painful memories.</i>

00:24.940 --> 00:26.530
<i>And these odd similarities</i>

00:26.690 --> 00:28.780
<i>between Maya
and Molly's style of flying</i>

00:28.950 --> 00:30.860
<i>have only added to my confusion.</i>

01:31.630 --> 01:34.390
<i>As long as we can fly,
we still have a chance.</i>

01:34.550 --> 01:37.180
<i>I refuse to believe
it's the end of the world.</i>

01:37.350 --> 01:38.930
<i>Mommy's really the best.</i>

01:39.100 --> 01:41.060
<i>Nothing could ever
happen to her.</i>

01:41.810 --> 01:43.020
<i>Yes, I can see her.</i>

01:43.190 --> 01:45.360
<i>She's winning! She's winning!</i>

02:10.710 --> 02:12.590
How can it be snowing?

02:13.260 --> 02:16.050
I have no idea.
The temperature suddenly plummeted.

02:16.220 --> 02:18.310
Come on, Koji, we have to cover
the Whizzing Arrow 3.

02:25.270 --> 02:27.440
-You guys want a hand?
-We're fine.

02:27.610 --> 02:29.570
Go get some sleep.
You need to rest.

02:29.860 --> 02:31.610
You'll find heaters
in the storage area.

02:47.080 --> 02:48.630
Great, a snow storm.

02:48.790 --> 02:51.170
As if being last in the ranking
wasn't enough.

02:56.130 --> 02:58.470
Hurry, Jordan,
I can't feel my fingers.

02:59.640 --> 03:01.720
Why are these things
such a pain to light?

03:02.180 --> 03:05.810
You would think by the end
of the 21st century... ah, yes!

03:06.020 --> 03:08.400
Oh man, I can't believe
it's so cold.

03:08.560 --> 03:10.190
It's freezing in here.

03:12.070 --> 03:14.490
Uh, here, climb in.

03:15.070 --> 03:18.240
Maybe we should sit, uhh,
closer to one another.

03:20.620 --> 03:24.120
Uh, like they say,
one Eskimo under a blanket freezes.

03:24.290 --> 03:26.540
Two Eskimos under a blanket live.

03:26.870 --> 03:29.920
Well, this Eskimo dies.

03:35.260 --> 03:36.880
I want to contact Earth.

03:37.050 --> 03:39.720
When is the next available window
for transmission?

03:39.890 --> 03:42.350
<i>Communication links presently open.</i>

03:42.810 --> 03:45.140
Very well.
Please contact...

03:46.270 --> 03:48.310
the Stern Boarding School.

03:53.570 --> 03:55.610
Do you know what time it is?

03:55.780 --> 03:58.950
Boarders cannot
receive calls at this hour!

03:59.160 --> 04:01.780
I'm sorry but I'm calling...

04:02.280 --> 04:03.580
long-distance.

04:04.240 --> 04:05.580
They all say that.

04:06.000 --> 04:09.250
Who is it you want to talk to?
The students are all asleep.

04:09.710 --> 04:12.880
I would like to speak
to Miss Eva Wei.

04:13.090 --> 04:15.960
Eva? Ha-ha!
What did she do?

04:16.130 --> 04:17.420
Steal from your shop?

04:17.590 --> 04:19.970
Leave her hotel room
without paying for it?

04:20.140 --> 04:21.470
Why, no.

04:21.640 --> 04:23.640
I just need to speak to her.

04:24.510 --> 04:26.220
It's been a long time.

04:26.560 --> 04:28.890
I'm Eva's father, Mr. Wei.

04:29.560 --> 04:31.770
What? Mr. Wei?
Don't worry.

04:31.940 --> 04:33.610
We'll find your sweet Eva.

04:33.770 --> 04:35.440
I'm sure she's fine.

04:35.610 --> 04:37.940
And about those payments,
I assure you,

04:38.110 --> 04:39.910
we were going to return them
as soon as possible.

04:40.280 --> 04:41.490
What are you talking about?

04:41.780 --> 04:43.490
You mean you haven't heard?

04:43.700 --> 04:48.410
On her birthday, she was up
all night waiting for your call.

04:49.210 --> 04:51.370
By morning, she just ran off.

04:53.500 --> 04:54.500
<i>Eva...</i>

05:29.540 --> 05:30.790
<i>Wow...</i>

05:31.000 --> 05:33.170
I've never been
to the mountains before.

05:33.830 --> 05:36.380
But I guess this makes up for it.

05:38.260 --> 05:40.630
Large wide open spaces.

05:40.800 --> 05:44.590
That's exactly the terrain we need
for the Whizzing Arrow 3.

05:45.220 --> 05:46.390
I can do it.

05:46.850 --> 05:48.930
I'm going to win this race!

05:55.440 --> 05:57.900
I'm going to win the race today!

06:03.700 --> 06:05.200
Prince Aikka!

06:05.700 --> 06:06.870
Hey!

06:11.000 --> 06:15.540
Watch out, 'cause today is
my day to win, Prince Aikka.

06:21.630 --> 06:25.640
Your time of half-heartedness
is over, my dear prince.

06:26.220 --> 06:29.010
You're either with us
or against us.

06:29.470 --> 06:33.560
My friendship with the human team
is a personal matter.

06:33.730 --> 06:35.730
It has nothing to do
with the Crogs.

06:37.560 --> 06:40.110
I will not repeat myself.

06:44.150 --> 06:47.490
Kross, have you lost your mind?

06:58.460 --> 07:01.090
No, but you certainly have.

07:06.180 --> 07:07.010
Let him be.

07:07.340 --> 07:09.970
If we can't trust
the prince of Nourasia,

07:10.140 --> 07:12.890
how can we trust his people?

07:13.480 --> 07:15.020
Kross, stop it.

07:20.400 --> 07:21.860
What must I do?

07:58.730 --> 07:59.810
They're rushing
straight ahead.

08:00.230 --> 08:01.560
Any sign of the stone gates?

08:05.740 --> 08:07.780
Yes, there's only one.

08:08.570 --> 08:10.280
It looks like a sprint, Molly.

08:10.570 --> 08:11.780
Well, it's about time.

08:12.030 --> 08:14.240
Let's see if these booster drives
still work.

08:14.490 --> 08:15.410
Hang on, Molly.

08:15.580 --> 08:17.580
Let Koji check the fuel
at full throttle.

08:23.750 --> 08:24.670
OK, champ.

08:24.840 --> 08:27.170
You can step on it
in exactly 20 seconds.

08:29.090 --> 08:29.970
Roger that.

08:34.010 --> 08:36.310
Just as I suspected.

08:36.850 --> 08:39.940
These creatures of flesh and blood
are good at showing off,

08:40.100 --> 08:41.860
but little else.

08:51.610 --> 08:54.530
Prove to me that you're
a leader, young prince.

09:00.580 --> 09:01.670
Is he kidding?

09:02.250 --> 09:04.960
OK, Jordan. 10 seconds to go
before boosters.

09:05.380 --> 09:07.260
Molly, there is
something fishy going on.

09:07.420 --> 09:10.430
Aikka is right beside us
and he's loading an arrow.

09:10.760 --> 09:13.260
Relax, Jordan.
It's not like he's going to shoot us.

09:14.510 --> 09:15.760
It sure looks like it.

09:16.310 --> 09:17.930
But then again,
he does owe me one.

09:23.690 --> 09:24.690
Here we go.

09:26.520 --> 09:28.780
<i>Unsakai', nourama safar!</i>

09:32.280 --> 09:33.280
You double-crosser!

10:06.690 --> 10:09.320
Fourth race, still no points.

10:09.820 --> 10:11.990
I'm not sure we can recover.

10:13.860 --> 10:15.910
Oh, sweet prince.

10:16.070 --> 10:18.700
You'll pay for that and double.

10:18.910 --> 10:20.700
What are you all talking about?

10:21.000 --> 10:21.960
I'm not quitting.

10:22.120 --> 10:23.830
This race is not over.

10:24.000 --> 10:25.380
We can still score.

10:26.920 --> 10:27.750
We can still...

10:38.140 --> 10:40.390
Why? Why did he do that?

10:40.560 --> 10:42.430
It's every one for himself, Molly.

10:42.600 --> 10:44.560
The Ultimate Prize
is just too valuable.

10:45.020 --> 10:47.310
Return to the Flying Temple
immediately.

10:47.560 --> 10:48.610
It's all over.

10:49.110 --> 10:50.780
At least for today.

10:56.070 --> 10:57.490
Koji, did you pick that up?

10:57.660 --> 10:59.950
The gate indicator
now points to the ground.

11:02.040 --> 11:03.290
Affirmative.

11:03.540 --> 11:05.420
Probably went haywire
with the crash.

11:06.290 --> 11:07.250
I wouldn't worry about it.

11:24.930 --> 11:26.270
By Kramm!

11:30.270 --> 11:32.030
Am I dreaming,
or have they all missed the gate?

11:32.320 --> 11:33.360
What?

11:44.790 --> 11:46.660
Where is the gate!

12:01.510 --> 12:03.310
Jordan, can you do me a favor?

12:03.470 --> 12:04.930
You want me to hurt Aikka?

12:05.310 --> 12:07.350
Just shoot the ice for now.

12:07.730 --> 12:09.150
Yeah, good idea.

12:09.310 --> 12:11.110
That ought to calm me down.

12:33.250 --> 12:36.090
Aikka may have done us
a great favor, Jordan.

12:37.340 --> 12:39.090
We're back in the race!

12:52.940 --> 12:55.570
The gate was hidden
under the ice cap all along.

12:56.190 --> 12:57.530
Molly, you're a genius!

12:57.900 --> 12:59.860
I knew today was my day.

13:10.040 --> 13:13.380
I didn't expect the humans
to find the cave so soon,

13:13.540 --> 13:15.460
considering their small brains.

13:23.640 --> 13:25.220
It was too good to be true.

13:25.850 --> 13:27.640
Though I calculated
the possibility.

13:27.810 --> 13:29.850
Nothing can ever surprise me.

13:38.570 --> 13:39.610
How did he know?

13:40.240 --> 13:41.950
Which way I was going?

13:43.030 --> 13:44.820
Out of our way, toaster!

13:57.630 --> 13:59.510
Until now I kept
a low profile,

13:59.670 --> 14:02.340
meticulously accumulating data
on my adversaries.

14:02.720 --> 14:04.050
This guy's untouchable.

14:04.300 --> 14:08.100
At last the time has come to claim
my rightful place among you.

14:18.190 --> 14:20.150
No, not today.

14:20.360 --> 14:21.740
I won't let you.

14:25.740 --> 14:27.660
Resistance is futile.

14:28.660 --> 14:33.080
My super processors can predict
your next 100 moves in advance.

14:33.250 --> 14:36.630
No one can stop me now
from reaching the Ultimate Prize.

14:38.460 --> 14:39.630
Really?

14:39.880 --> 14:41.380
Predict this.

14:51.850 --> 14:52.930
Accept the truth!

14:53.430 --> 14:55.560
Your kind has had their time.

14:55.770 --> 14:59.360
Robots are the next step
in the chain of evolution!

15:12.410 --> 15:15.000
Today is my day.
You hear me?

15:22.000 --> 15:22.710
Fools!

15:23.090 --> 15:26.800
Unlike you, I can predict
the fall of each of these blocks.

15:58.790 --> 16:01.590
So many possibilities.

16:02.920 --> 16:04.840
It's beautiful.

16:06.010 --> 16:07.130
Faster! Faster!

16:27.650 --> 16:30.240
What a race, my friends.
What a race!

16:32.280 --> 16:35.580
Sweet Molly finally scores.
And what a score.

16:35.750 --> 16:38.790
A big nine points for her first place.

16:39.210 --> 16:41.250
Bravo, Molly!

16:43.590 --> 16:46.170
As for the second
and third place, well...

16:46.420 --> 16:49.220
all the others seemed
to have given up on the hidden gate.

16:51.800 --> 16:55.100
I'm not sure the Earth team
made many new friends today.

16:56.060 --> 16:58.560
But that's the law
of the Great Race.

17:00.650 --> 17:05.150
Only the most worthy
can claim the Ultimate Prize.

17:06.030 --> 17:07.490
Yeah!

17:14.160 --> 17:15.280
Bravo.

17:17.830 --> 17:18.620
Thank you, sir.

17:26.710 --> 17:28.800
You better believe it.
Of course he tried to.

17:28.970 --> 17:30.760
Or rather it tried to.

17:30.930 --> 17:33.720
But the day a tin can
gets the better of me, I quit.

17:42.400 --> 17:45.650
Now what I'd like to see
is the face of good ol' Prince Aikka.

17:45.820 --> 17:48.230
He must be eating
his bow by now.

17:58.950 --> 18:01.410
It looks like
we have a clear night tonight.

18:01.620 --> 18:02.710
You're right.

18:07.920 --> 18:11.630
I've never had a chance
to ask you much about your life.

18:14.090 --> 18:18.470
So, do you have any brothers
and sisters waiting back on Earth?

18:21.020 --> 18:23.310
I see. An only child.

18:24.020 --> 18:26.230
Your parents must have
smothered you.

18:29.030 --> 18:31.780
Where were you working
before you joined the team?

18:32.030 --> 18:33.490
Working?

18:33.650 --> 18:35.450
Yes, as a mechanic.

18:35.620 --> 18:37.740
That's what you were doing before,
wasn't it?

18:37.910 --> 18:40.790
Yes, of course, a mechanic.

18:41.200 --> 18:43.290
Well, there were several places.

18:43.460 --> 18:46.130
The last one was...

18:46.790 --> 18:48.790
<i>Brokaw Motor-Racing.
Yeah.</i>

18:49.300 --> 18:51.420
Brokaro Motor-Racing?

18:53.880 --> 18:57.220
I happen to know
Clive Brokaro quite well.

18:57.390 --> 18:59.810
He worked for me
for several years,

19:00.060 --> 19:02.640
after his racing team
went bankrupt.

19:03.980 --> 19:06.150
Well, I... I mean...

19:06.310 --> 19:09.320
Look, I worked...
Who cares where.

19:09.570 --> 19:11.480
Listen here,
have you ever heard

19:11.650 --> 19:13.690
of the Stern Boarding School,
young lady?

19:17.240 --> 19:19.660
Stern Boarding?

19:24.250 --> 19:26.330
I'll be more direct.

19:27.210 --> 19:29.540
Are you my daughter, Eva?

19:38.260 --> 19:41.260
If I were your daughter,
you would know it immediately.

19:41.510 --> 19:44.350
I mean, you really wouldn't need
to ask me, would you ?

19:46.270 --> 19:47.850
Now if you'll excuse me,

19:48.020 --> 19:49.940
I'd like to go check
on the Whizzing Arrow.

19:50.110 --> 19:51.860
Great day today, huh?

20:05.160 --> 20:06.410
Uh, Molly, wait up.

20:07.750 --> 20:09.580
The old man didn't fight
with you again, did he?

20:09.750 --> 20:12.420
Because if he did, I'm going
to have a few words with him.

20:12.590 --> 20:14.760
It wasn't exactly a fight.

20:22.680 --> 20:25.350
So what did you mean,
not exactly?

20:26.600 --> 20:29.850
Let's just say he found out
that I lied a little to get this job.

20:30.020 --> 20:32.650
I mean, like,
who doesn't, right?

20:37.700 --> 20:40.950
I think it's more than that.
Do you want to talk about it?

20:41.450 --> 20:44.240
It could help, you know.
I'd be more than happy to...

20:47.040 --> 20:48.660
Thanks, Jordan.

20:49.370 --> 20:51.830
But I'd rather go to bed now
if you don't mind.

21:02.180 --> 21:03.930
Goodnight, Molly.

21:05.140 --> 21:06.720
You were great today.

21:09.640 --> 21:11.400
<i>We'll be a family again.</i>

21:11.560 --> 21:13.150
<i>But not like this.</i>

21:13.520 --> 21:15.980
<i>Who would want
a father like that?</i>

21:16.150 --> 21:19.570
<i>I'd rather remain Molly
for the rest of my life.</i>

21:25.490 --> 21:26.740
Oh, Eva...

21:27.750 --> 21:29.250
It's you.
